Description: desktop API client for HTTP, WebSocket and GraphQL
 Rustman sends HTTP, WebSocket and GraphQL requests and shows the responses,
 in the manner of Postman, without an account or a cloud service. Requests
 live in collections with environments, history, pre-request and test
 scripts, and can be imported from curl, OpenAPI and Postman. A collection
 directory can be a git repository, committed and pushed from the app; the
 remote operations need git installed.
 .
 HTML responses are shown as readable text and can be opened in the web browser.
 .
 This build leaves out the in-app updater: apt delivers updates.
